{"name":"Black Boudoir","hex":"#454749","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"boudoir","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman's private sitting room, dressing room, or bedroom.","An army tent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boudoir"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boudoir","blocks":[{"text":"A boudoir is a lady’s private sitting room or salon in a furnished residence, usually between the dining room and the bedroom, but can also refer to a lady’s private bedroom. The term derives from the French verb bouder or adjective boudeur (sulking)—the room was originally a space to withdraw to."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Poland_Niebor%C3%B3w_Palace_008.jpg/330px-Poland_Niebor%C3%B3w_Palace_008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudoir"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Boudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg/250px-Boudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Boudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg/330px-Boudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Boudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg/250px-Boudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoudoir_H%C3%B4tel_de_Besenval_Paris_II.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Boudoir.jpg/250px-Boudoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Boudoir.jpg/250px-Boudoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoudoir.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_Boudoir_%28Louis_XVI._Period%29.jpg/250px-A_Boudoir_%28Louis_XVI._Period%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_Boudoir_%28Louis_XVI._Period%29.jpg/500px-A_Boudoir_%28Louis_XVI._Period%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_Boudoir_%28Louis_XVI._Period%29.jpg/250px-A_Boudoir_%28Louis_XVI._Period%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o